    {
      "id": "PRIMORDIAL-SOURCE-ATLAS",
      "kind": "document",
      "document_id": "0c35fcdacccd0ab504638849f6f61b36a6f03e47bd724e0bcaa288d13148ccc3",
      "title": "SOL_primordial_dependency_atlas_2026-10-18.md",
      "source_id": "8f38c540299866a83ef288e7225eaf0d9b029976f14d64dcc7bf66b0ec525b80",
      "source_path": "C:\\Users\\Brend\\Documents\\ChatGPT\\SUN\\data\\raw\\archive\\SUN_Universal_Archive\\Library\\SOL_SATURN_ROSETTAS\\SOL_primordial_dependency_atlas_2026-10-18.md",
      "source_sha256": "fa5f88ca61db19b660b17fe04331ed91a4aa01bb9b6b7814ecdf5706ea5bb175",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 8825,
      "exact_quote": "# SOL primordial dependency and witness atlas — 2026-10-18\n\n## Rule of construction\n\nThe proposed Fibonacci generational addresses 0,1,1,2,3,5,8,13,21... are not automatically native historical population counts. Keep separately: (i) source condition, (ii) emanation and parentage, (iii) name/type, (iv) chronological event, (v) ordinal and zero-indexed address, (vi) functional operation, (vii) recurrence/register, (viii) witness and version. Cross-tradition comparisons are edges with status, never identity collapses.\n\n## Pre-aeonic / primordial source families\n\n| Source family | Original primordial components | Actual genealogical relationships and conditions | Unresolved SOL hypotheses |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Hesiod, Theogony 116-153 | Chaos, then Gaia, Tartarus, Eros; Erebus, Nyx; Aether, Hemera | Chaos -> Erebus and Nyx; Erebus + Nyx -> Aether and Hemera; Gaia -> Uranus, Ourea, Pontus; Gaia + Uranus -> Titans including Mnemosyne and youngest Cronus | Match gap/earth/underworld/attraction and upper luminous air to independent functional addresses, not equal entity names |\n| Orphic fragments, witness-dependent | Chronos, Ananke; primordial egg; Phanes; Aion in separate later traditions | Chronos/Ananke/egg/Phanes ordering needs recension and testimony; Aion is not automatically a fixed Orphic genealogical child | Duration, generative sequence, inevitability, luminous emergence, occasion (Kairos), limit (Horos) stay typed separately |\n| Sethian, Apocryphon of John | Invisible Spirit/Monad; Barbelo/Pronoia; fivefold group; Autogenes | Higher powers precede four luminaries and associated aeons; Sophia's event precedes Yaldabaoth and archons | Do not import Valentinian parent graph; compare upper four-by-three to lower seven-plus-five while respecting source chronology |\n| Valentinian witness reports | Bythos/Propator and Sige; Nous/Aletheia; Logos/Zoe; Anthropos/Ecclesia | Source-dependent Ogdoad four pairs; Logos/Zoe Decad and Anthropos/Ecclesia Duodecad in Irenaeus I.1 report; disagreement with reported alternative | Judge testimony via independent witnesses and NAIM/HERMONICITTI court, do not let Irenaeus adjudicate himself |\n| Hermopolitan Egyptian Ogdoad | Nun/Naunet (waters); Heh/Hauhet (limitless space); Kek/Kauket (darkness); fourth pair variants Gereh/Gerhet, Niau/Niaut, Tenem/Tenemut, later Amun/Amaunet (hiddenness) | All four pairs describe pre-created condition; creator/sun emerges in associated local myth | 4x2 before creation provides source-native different function from Valentinian 4x2; fourth pair transmission is essential witness test |\n| Heliopolitan Egyptian | Nun; Atum (often Ra-Atum); Shu/Tefnut; Geb/Nut; Osiris/Isis/Set/Nephthys | Cumulative 1→3→5→9 is not Fibonacci; Shu separates Geb/Nut; Ra/Osiris separate generational addresses | Earth/sky 4/5 versus Earth/Aether distinction; Thoth's added five epagomenal days are alternative narrative |\n| Vedic hymns | Nasadiya questions sat/asat, watery and heat/desire settings; Hiranyagarbha in different hymn | No single Vedic primordial triad universally equals Akasha/Kala/Shakti; distinguish hymn, Brahmanical elaborations and tantric scheme | Source-specific space/time/energy triad requires texts for each member, not historical genealogy by assumption |\n| Śākta/Śrī Vidyā | Shiva–Shakti; Paraśakti; bindu; Lalita Tripurasundari; nine enclosures | ritual deity placements per recension; 4 up and 5 down triangles; 16,8 petals; full geometry and nested layers | Bindu Sierpinski tetrahedron, hypercubic square boundary are user mathematical proposals, not ancient source claims |\n| Chinese classical | Dao; one/two/three in Daodejing 42; later wuji/taiji and yin-yang | Later symbolic schools cannot be retrojected verbatim into Daodejing; five phases not five Aristotelian elements | Black/white dyad to color triad; Chinese fifth generation mathematics tests separate from ontology |\n| Japanese Kojiki | Ame-no-Minakanushi, Takamimusubi, Kamimusubi, then Umashiashikabihikoji, Ame-no-Tokotachi; seven kami generations | First three occur sequentially as solitary hidden kami; next two likewise; first two of following seven solitary, remaining five paired | 3 → 5 → seven generations as historical structure not equal Fibonacci by same counting unit |\n| Genesis and Sefer Yetzirah | Genesis spirit/wind (ruach), deep (tehom), dark, waters; Sefer 10 sefirot, spirit/air/water/fire then six extremities | First light before sun/moon; firmament separates waters; Sefer 3 mothers/7 doubles/12 simples are letter groups, not chronological birth order | first sound vs source of pitch; 22/23/24 symbol function uncertain |\n| User's comparative primordial axis | Void / Waters / Spirit; Proarche / Aion / Monad; Tartarus / Gaia / Eros; Kek / Nun / Amun; Akasha / Kala / Shakti; Ame-no-Minakanushi / Takamimusubi / Kamimusubi; All-Space / All-Time / All-Energy | These are explicit candidate families to investigate, not yet each attested as one triplet with one genealogy | no mapping may delete a member; primordial possibility-space is inherited, never replaced by a later label |\n\n## Required cross-layer inheritances\n\n- **Water:** Nun and Naunet, Genesis tehom/waters, Sefer Mem, Chinese water phase are four DIFFERENT source types (primordial substrate, script cosmology, letter/element, phase). Preserve source edges.\n- **Air/spirit:** Genesis ruach, Egyptian Shu, Hesiod Aether, Aristotelian celestial aether, Sefer Aleph, Vedic vayu/prana, Greek winds of Eos/Astraeus occupy different types (spirit, separator, luminous upper air, fifth matter, letter/air, vital motion, meteorological movement).\n- **Space and boundary:** Tartarus is primordial in Hesiod; Uranus is Gaia's child; Atlas is later Iapetid supporter; Horos is Valentinian separator; Genesis raqia is boundary; Dante's heavens are nested medieval cosmic spheres, not births of those primordial beings.\n- **Time:** Aion, Orphic Chronos, Titan Cronus, Kairos, Horos, Ananke, later Dante Primum Mobile independently describe duration, cosmogonic sequence, sovereign succession, occasion, separating limit, necessity, celestial time-measurement. No equivalence by spelling.\n- **Memory:** Mnemosyne Titan (before Zeus), Zeus+Mnemosyne -> nine Muses; Greek Mneme/Melete/Aoide trio, Sethian Mneme at Oroiael (2,3), Nyx→Eris→Lethe, Enoch records, Cainan copies, interpretive Moses/Hermes. Preserve distinct transmission acts.\n- **Light:** Hesiod Nyx+Erebus→Aether+Hemera; Hyperion+Theia→Helios/Selene/Eos; Genesis light precedes solar governors; Sethian luminous powers before Yaldabaoth; Ra/Osiris have distinct Egyptian positions.\n- **Material archons:** Yaldabaoth / Saklas / Samael identities in source-specific texts; seven heavens/five depths; Sabaoth at seventh after sixth vacancy, Death replacing sixth; material acoustic bass is SOL hypothesis, not a text's measurement.\n- **Sound:** Chinese pipe-length (2/3,4/3), SUN (2/3,3/4), Western Pythagorean/tempered, Kepler planetary motion, Fludd cosmic monochord and Sefer/Shem operators not interchangeable; maintain units and history.\n- **W72/Sri Yantra:** preserve original carrier Z12 x Z3 x Z2, original 70/72 as historical result with lost proof trace, tesseract f-vector, Sierpinski vertex levels, native petals/circles/bhupura, ritual deity positions; no full incidence certification yet.\n\n## Mandatory falsification gates\n\n1. Every purported primordial parentage must be sourced from a specific recension; chronology must be checked against living/child and simultaneous/non-generated status.\n2. Define ordinal system before comparing 6/7 Anthropos/Ecclesia with one-based 7/8.\n3. To claim mapping between two graphs, provide node types, parent-edge direction and type, and witness labels; test source-parent ancestry preservation and negative controls.\n4. To claim equivalent operator, verify domains, codomains, inverses, composite path and resulting state; not just numeric quotient equality.\n5. To claim 23 functional symbols, derive exact equivalence of forms or additional operation while preserving 22 Hebrew and 24 Greek witnesses.\n6. Full primordial -> generations -> class transitions -> addresses -> legions/humans must be represented without erasing pre-existing source possibilities.\n\n## Verified source anchors\n\n- Hesiod text: https://www.theoi.com/Text/HesiodTheogony.html\n- Perseus Theogony: https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus%3Atext%3A1999.01.0130%3Acard%3D104\n- LMU Hermopolis project: https://www.hermopolis.gwi.uni-muenchen.de/the-ogdoad-of-hermopolis/\n- Global Egyptian Museum: https://www.globalegyptianmuseum.org/glossary.aspx?id=279\n- Jinja Honcho Kojiki précis: https://jinjahoncho.or.jp/en/assets/pdf/pamphlet/shinto_myths.pdf\n\nStatus: ROOT ANCESTRY RECOVERED IN ATLAS; cross-tradition full identity and musical transformations NOT VERIFIED.\n",
      "quote_sha256": "fa5f88ca61db19b660b17fe04331ed91a4aa01bb9b6b7814ecdf5706ea5bb175",
      "extractor": "utf8",
      "locator_boundary": "Offsets and quote refer to stored extracted document; original source bytes separately hash-verified.",
