    "rows": {
      "goetia_de_laurence_1916": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Bael",
          "legions_primary": 66,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 1,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(1.) Bael. —The First Principal Spirit is a King ruling\r\nin the East, called Bael. He maketh thee to go\r\nInvisible. He ruleth over 66 Legions of Infernal Spirits.\r\nHe appeareth in divers shapes, sometimes like a Cat,\r\nsometimes like a Toad, and sometimes like a Man, and\r\nsometimes all these forms at once. He speaketh hoarsely.\r\nThis is his character which is used to be worn as a\r\nLamen before him who calleth him forth, or else he will\r\nnot do thee homage.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "199ef341a14c91a9c3c719593b4b7ac8924e423a1d1c7b8d4dbff7b197b15b8e",
          "count_context": "King ruling in the East, called Bael. He maketh thee to go Invisible. He ruleth over 66 Legions of Infernal Spirits. He appeareth in divers shapes, so",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Agares",
          "legions_primary": 31,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 2,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(2.) Agares. —The Second Spirit is a Duke called\r\nAgreas, or Agares. He is under the Power of the East,\r\nand cometh up in the form of an old fair Man, riding\r\nupon a Crocodile, carrying a Goshawk upon his fist, and\r\nyet mild in appearance. He maketh them to run that\r\nstand still, and bringeth back runaways. He teaches all\r\nLanguages or Tongues presently. He hath power also\r\nto destroy Dignities both Spiritual and Temporal, and\r\ncauseth Earthquakes. He was of the Order of Virtues.\r\nHe hath under his government 31 Legions of Spirits.\r\nAnd this is his Seal or Character which thou shalt wear\r\nas a Lamen before thee.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "1afdcafa8ff8209cdf6652bfdd4d74ec1e759665cd591a777e308545e38a7b7d",
          "count_context": "nd causeth Earthquakes. He was of the Order of Virtues. He hath under his government 31 Legions of Spirits. And this is his Seal or Character which th",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 3,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Vassago",
          "legions_primary": 26,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 3,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(3.) Vassago. —The Third Spirit is a Mighty Prince,\r\nbeing of the same nature as Agares. He is called\r\nVassago. This Spirit is of a Good Nature, and his office\r\nis to declare things Past and to Come, and to discover all\r\nthings Hid or Lost. And he governeth 26 Legions of\r\nSpirits, and this is his Seal.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "620208f6fa7ecfb6ffbf131ec7816d5b2c71999395feea5f3b610251da2f85fd",
          "count_context": "re things Past and to Come, and to discover all things Hid or Lost. And he governeth 26 Legions of Spirits, and this is his Seal.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 4,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Samigina",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 4,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(4.) Samigina , or Gamigin .—The Fourth Spirit is\r\nSamigina, a Great Marquis. He appeareth in the form of a little Horse or Ass, and then into Human shape\r\ndoth he change himself at the request of the Master. He\r\nspeaketh with a hoarse voice. He ruleth over 30 Legions\r\nof Inferiors. He teaches all Liberal Sciences, and giveth\r\naccount of Dead Souls that died in sin. And his Seal is\r\nthis, which is to be worn before the Magician when he is\r\nInvocator, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "eb0abeb9f42db69f2db2d8ed928d30224497760a83758c543b183a91654b576f",
          "count_context": "imself at the request of the Master. He speaketh with a hoarse voice. He ruleth over 30 Legions of Inferiors. He teaches all Liberal Sciences, and giv",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 5,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Marbas",
          "legions_primary": 36,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 5,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(5.) Marbas. —The fifth Spirit is Marbas. He is a\r\nGreat President, and appeareth at first in the form of a\r\nGreat Lion, but afterwards, at the request of the Master,\r\nhe putteth on Human Shape. He answereth truly of\r\nthings Hidden or Secret. He causeth Diseases and\r\ncureth them. Again, he giveth great Wisdom and Knowledge\r\nin Mechanical Arts; and can change men into other\r\nshapes. He governeth 36 Legions of Spirits. And his\r\nSeal is this, which is to be worn as aforesaid.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "beefcc10042aeb30ae8a2edbd804d27c72c2b4db97fe64aa509ac68ad47a7928",
          "count_context": "and Knowledge in Mechanical Arts; and can change men into other shapes. He governeth 36 Legions of Spirits. And his Seal is this, which is to be worn ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 6,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Valefor",
          "legions_primary": 10,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 6,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(6.) Valefor. —The Sixth Spirit is Valefor. He is a\r\nmighty Duke, and appeareth in the shape of a Lion with\r\nan Ass’s Head, bellowing. He is a good Familiar, but\r\ntempteth them he is a familiar of to steal. He governeth\r\n10 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, which is to be\r\nworn, whether thou wilt have him for a Familiar, or not.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "a8ffb20f4f016592e0f2ea7d55aa74e9078eb45e8bef1a16c452e56e9db0e9f3",
          "count_context": " He is a good Familiar, but tempteth them he is a familiar of to steal. He governeth 10 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, which is to be worn, whe",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 7,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Amon",
          "legions_primary": 40,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 7,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(7.) Amon. —The Seventh Spirit is Amon. He is a\r\nMarquis great in power, and most stern. He appeareth\r\nlike a Wolf with a Serpent’s tail, vomiting out of his\r\nmouth flames of fire; but at the command of the Magician\r\nhe putteth on the shape of a Man with Dog’s teeth beset\r\nin a head like a Raven; or else like a Man with a Raven’s\r\nhead (simply). He telleth all things Past and to Come.\r\nHe procureth feuds and reconcileth controversies between\r\nfriends. He governeth 40 Legions of Spirits. His\r\nSeal is this which is to be worn as aforesaid, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "28ed558a737278a3164d7fa13406188364173e9cd2241a5c3b5f881c2467da7e",
          "count_context": "Come. He procureth feuds and reconcileth controversies between friends. He governeth 40 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this which is to be worn as af",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 8,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Barbatos",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 8,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(8.) Barbatos. —The Eighth Spirit is Barbatos. He\r\nis a Great Duke, and appeareth when the Sun is in Sagittary, with four noble Kings and their companies of\r\ngreat troops. He giveth understanding of the singing\r\nof Birds, and of the Voices of other creatures, such as\r\nthe barking of Dogs. He breaketh the Hidden Treasures\r\nopen that have been laid by the Enchantments of\r\nMagicians. He is of the Order of Virtues, of which some\r\npart he retaineth still; and he knoweth all things Past,\r\nand to come, and conciliateth Friends and those that be\r\nin Power. He ruleth over 30 Legions of Spirits. His\r\nSeal of Obedience is this, the which wear before thee as\r\naforesaid.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "6cd41cc4de02cea44256fa0ea55fb8292a88345185c23007d0b24f06b4087aff",
          "count_context": "st, and to come, and conciliateth Friends and those that be in Power. He ruleth over 30 Legions of Spirits. His Seal of Obedience is this, the which w",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 9,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Paimon",
          "legions_primary": 200,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": 25,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 9,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(9) Paimon. —The Ninth Spirit in this Order is\r\nPaimon, a Great King, and very obedient unto Lucifer .\r\nHe appeareth in the form of a Man sitting upon a\r\nDromedary with a Crown most glorious upon his head.\r\nThere goeth before him also an Host of Spirits, like Men\r\nwith Trumpets and well sounding Cymbals, and all other\r\nsorts of Musical Instruments. He hath a great Voice,\r\nand roareth at his first coming, and his speech is such\r\nthat the Magician cannot well understand unless he can\r\ncompel him. This Spirit can teach all Arts and Sciences,\r\nand other secret things. He can discover unto thee what\r\nthe Earth is, and what holdeth it up in the Waters; and\r\nwhat Mind is, and where it is; or any other thing thou\r\nmayest desire to know. He giveth Dignity, and confirmeth\r\nthe same. He bindeth or maketh any man subject\r\nunto the Magician if he so desire it. He giveth good\r\nFamiliars, and such as can teach all Arts. He is to be\r\nobserved towards the West. He is of the Order of Dominations. He hath under him 200 Legions of Spirits,\r\nand part of them are of the Order of Angels, and the\r\nother part of Potentates. Now if thou callest this Spirit\r\nPaimon alone, thou must make him some offering; and there will attend him two Kings called Labal and Abalim , and also other Spirits who be of the Order of\r\nPotentates in his Host, and 25 Legions. And those\r\nSpirits which be subject unto them are not always with\r\nthem unless the Magician do compel them. His Character\r\nis this which must be worn as a Lamen before thee,\r\netc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "cd7b5de8389c67132f2c041c245addf5d9455a0dfe4f8a4cb48b0ed6d8461d1e",
          "count_context": "o be observed towards the West. He is of the Order of Dominations. He hath under him 200 Legions of Spirits, and part of them are of the Order of Angel",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 10,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Buer",
          "legions_primary": 50,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 10,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(10.) Buer. —The Tenth Spirit is Buer, a Great President.\r\nHe appeareth in Sagittary, and that is his shape\r\nwhen the Sun is there. He teaches Philosophy, both\r\nMoral and Natural, and the Logic Art, and also the Virtues\r\nof all Herbs and Plants. He healeth all distempers\r\nin man, and giveth good Familiars. He governeth 50\r\nLegions of Spirits, and his Character of obedience is\r\nthis, which thou must wear when thou callest him forth\r\nunto appearance.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "a886f45755ebd988b086955de0d7245a32625a06b9908ff45513fdb709e8abfd",
          "count_context": "nd Plants. He healeth all distempers in man, and giveth good Familiars. He governeth 50 Legions of Spirits, and his Character of obedience is this, wh",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 11,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Gusion",
          "legions_primary": 40,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 11,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(11.) Gusion. —The Eleventh Spirit in order is a\r\ngreat and strong Duke, called Gusion. He appeareth\r\nlike a Xenopilus. He telleth all things, Past, Present,\r\nand to Come, and showeth the meaning and resolution\r\nof all questions thou mayest ask. He conciliateth and\r\nreconcileth friendships, and giveth Honour and Dignity\r\nunto any. He ruleth over 40 Legions of Spirits. His\r\nSeal is this, the which wear thou as aforesaid.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "82aeaa3eb97bee2500cdf9856e1dc757a6dbe5c5e81823fcd6ed98f25e5b83e8",
          "count_context": " and reconcileth friendships, and giveth Honour and Dignity unto any. He ruleth over 40 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, the which wear thou as a",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 12,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Sitri",
          "legions_primary": 60,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 12,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(12.) Sitri. —The Twelfth Spirit is Sitri. He is a\r\nGreat Prince and appeareth at first with a Leopard’s\r\nhead and the Wings of a Gryphon, but after the command\r\nof the Master of the Exorcism he putteth on\r\nHuman shape, and that very beautiful. He enflameth\r\nmen with Women’s love, and Women with Men’s love;\r\nand causeth them also to show themselves naked if it be\r\ndesired. He governeth 60 Legions of Spirits. His Seal\r\nis this, to be worn as a Lamen before thee, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "5b74416fac0702d66205ff4cc0084f38308e156c86c98309ed15030ee753463a",
          "count_context": " love; and causeth them also to show themselves naked if it be desired. He governeth 60 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, to be worn as a Lamen be",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 13,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Beleth",
          "legions_primary": 85,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 13,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(13.) Beleth. —The Thirteenth Spirit is called Beleth (or Bileth, or Bilet). He is a mighty King and terrible.\r\nHe rideth on a pale horse with trumpets and other kinds\r\nof musical instruments playing before him. He is very\r\nfurious at his first appearance, that is, while the Exorcist\r\nlayeth his courage; for to do this he must hold a\r\nHazel Wand in his hand, striking it out towards the\r\nSouth and East Quarters, make a triangle, △, without\r\nthe Circle, and then command him into it by the Bonds\r\nand Charges of Spirits as hereafter followeth. And if\r\nhe doth not enter into the triangle, △, at your threats,\r\nrehearse the Bonds and Charms before him, and then\r\nhe will yield Obedience and come into it, and do what\r\nhe is commanded by the Exorcist. Yet he must receive\r\nhim courteously because he is a Great King, and do homage\r\nunto him, as the Kings and Princes do that attend\r\nupon him. And thou must have always a Silver Ring\r\non the middle finger of the left hand held against thy\r\nface, as they do yet before Amaymon . This Great King\r\nBeleth causeth all the love that may be, both of Men and\r\nof Women, until the Master Exorcist hath had his desire\r\nfulfilled. He is of the Order of Powers, and he governeth\r\n85 Legions of Spirits. His Noble Seal is this, which is\r\nto be worn before thee at working.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "ab9b8e78f2a5439367e8a2e2871489113f553ff84f10486665e8c6f3dca0fa18",
          "count_context": "orcist hath had his desire fulfilled. He is of the Order of Powers, and he governeth 85 Legions of Spirits. His Noble Seal is this, which is to be wor",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 14,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Leraje",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 14,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(14.) Leraje , or Leraikha .—The Fourteenth Spirit\r\nis called Leraje (or Leraie). He is a Marquis Great in\r\nPower, showing himself in the likeness of an Archer clad\r\nin Green, and carrying a Bow and Quiver. He causeth\r\nall great Battles and Contests; and maketh wounds to\r\nputrefy that are made with Arrows by Archers. This\r\nbelongeth unto Sagittary. He governeth 30 Legions of\r\nSpirits, and this is his Seal, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "c4c990e7afa6bef96d74a12658c934e763454dc5823b3e8102d688e77f6a78ae",
          "count_context": "fy that are made with Arrows by Archers. This belongeth unto Sagittary. He governeth 30 Legions of Spirits, and this is his Seal, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 15,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Eligos",
          "legions_primary": 60,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 15,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(15.) Eligos. —The Fifteenth Spirit in Order is\r\nEligos, a Great Duke, and appeareth in the form of a\r\ngoodly Knight, carrying a Lance, an Ensign, and a Serpent.\r\nHe discovereth hidden things, and knoweth things\r\nto come; and of Wars, and how the Soldiers will or shall\r\nmeet. He causeth the Love of Lords and Great Persons.\r\nHe governeth 60 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "7ad28909e6c6b768923240e069364aab600d2667bdf31de5d3de876a0b9d3597",
          "count_context": "ers will or shall meet. He causeth the Love of Lords and Great Persons. He governeth 60 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
