            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(19.) Sallos. —The Nineteenth Spirit is Sallos (or\r\nSaleos). He is a Great and Mighty Duke, and appeareth\r\nin the form of a gallant Soldier riding on a Crocodile,\r\nwith a Ducal Crown on his head, but peaceably. He causeth the Love of Women to Men, and of Men to\r\nWomen; and governeth 30 Legions of Spirits. His Seal\r\nis this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "bf413c73ed5574eb6c403a815f997e1b3ca5b9b698ec746c925e5c12eab75a5e",
          "count_context": "t peaceably. He causeth the Love of Women to Men, and of Men to Women; and governeth 30 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 20,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Purson",
          "legions_primary": 22,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 20,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(20.) Purson. —The Twentieth Spirit is Purson, a\r\nGreat King. His appearance is comely, like a Man with\r\na Lion’s face, carrying a cruel Viper in his hand, and\r\nriding upon a Bear. Going before him are many Trumpets\r\nsounding. He knoweth all things hidden, and\r\ncan discover Treasure, and tell all things Past, Present,\r\nand to Come. He can take a Body either Human or\r\nAërial, and answereth truly of all Earthly things both\r\nSecret and Divine, and of the Creation of the World.\r\nHe bringeth forth good Familiars, and under his Government\r\nthere be 22 Legions of Spirits, partly of the\r\nOrder of Virtues and partly of the Order of Thrones.\r\nHis Mark, Seal, or Character is this, unto the which he\r\noweth obedience, and which thou shalt wear in time of\r\naction, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "cba9863b766a79d1807b12f3e5d42dc71249562e7a01106cad896b8ab2054809",
          "count_context": "on of the World. He bringeth forth good Familiars, and under his Government there be 22 Legions of Spirits, partly of the Order of Virtues and partly ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 21,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Marax",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
