            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(27.) Ronové. —The Twenty-seventh Spirit is Ronové.\r\nHe appeareth in the Form of a Monster. He teacheth\r\nthe Art of Rhetoric very well and giveth Good Servants,\r\nKnowledge of Tongues, and Favours with Friends or\r\nFoes. He is a Marquis and Great Earl; and there be\r\nunder his command 19 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is\r\nthis, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "b8144b52b7e9f9c4414cde57be6335a9ec011541fda1a5c821c70603519cfb56",
          "count_context": "with Friends or Foes. He is a Marquis and Great Earl; and there be under his command 19 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 28,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Berith",
          "legions_primary": 26,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 28,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(28.) Berith. —The Twenty-eighth Spirit in Order,\r\nas Solomon bound them, is named Berith. He is a\r\nMighty, Great, and Terrible Duke. He hath two other\r\nNames given unto him by men of later times, viz.: Beale ,\r\nor Beal , and Bofry or Bolfry . He appeareth in the\r\nForm of a Soldier with Red Clothing, riding upon a Red\r\nHorse, and having a Crown of Gold upon his head. He\r\ngiveth true answers, Past, Present, and to Come. Thou\r\nmust make use of a Ring in calling him forth, as is before\r\nspoken of regarding Beleth. He can turn all metals\r\ninto Gold. He can give Dignities, and can confirm them\r\nunto Man. He speaketh with a very clear and subtle\r\nVoice. He governeth 26 Legions of Spirits. His Seal\r\nis this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "eeab9a5085d83fefce447157a998baf54507c300683b8b05806ab3a6b786512a",
          "count_context": " confirm them unto Man. He speaketh with a very clear and subtle Voice. He governeth 26 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 29,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Astaroth",
          "legions_primary": 40,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 29,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(29.) Astaroth. —The Twenty-ninth Spirit is Astaroth.\r\nHe is a Mighty, Strong Duke, and appeareth in the Form of an hurtful Angel riding on an Infernal\r\nBeast like a Dragon, and carrying in his right hand a\r\nViper. Thou must in no wise let him approach too near\r\nunto thee, lest he do thee damage by his Noisome Breath.\r\nWherefore the Magician must hold the Magical Ring\r\nnear his face, and that will defend him. He giveth true\r\nanswers of things Past, Present, and to Come, and can\r\ndiscover all Secrets. He will declare wittingly how the\r\nSpirits fell, if desired, and the reason of his own fall.\r\nHe can make men wonderfully knowing in all Liberal\r\nSciences. He ruleth 40 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is\r\nthis, which wear thou as a Lamen before thee, or else he\r\nwill not appear nor yet obey thee, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "6100681a238ef53a014c24ee3957c875d1c8d518e2b04d8a213538bdcf87b2ae",
          "count_context": "his own fall. He can make men wonderfully knowing in all Liberal Sciences. He ruleth 40 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, which wear thou as a Lam",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 30,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Forneus",
          "legions_primary": 29,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 30,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(30.) Forneus. —The Thirtieth Spirit is Forneus. He\r\nis a Mighty and Great Marquis, and appeareth in the\r\nForm of a Great Sea-Monster. He teacheth, and maketh\r\nmen wonderfully knowing in the Art of Rhetoric. He\r\ncauseth men to have a Good Name, and to have the knowledge\r\nand understanding of Tongues. He maketh one to\r\nbe beloved of his Foes as well as of his Friends. He\r\ngoverneth 29 Legions of Spirits, partly of the Order of\r\nThrones, and partly of that of Angels. His Seal is this,\r\nwhich wear thou, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "d407d2edf47a2b4d19518bdc4ff7fca6e5277819b65de69c3c5d1714cdebef5f",
          "count_context": "ues. He maketh one to be beloved of his Foes as well as of his Friends. He governeth 29 Legions of Spirits, partly of the Order of Thrones, and partly",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 31,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Foras",
          "legions_primary": 29,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 31,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(31.) Foras. —The Thirty-first Spirit is Foras. He\r\nis a Mighty President, and appeareth in the Form of a\r\nStrong Man in Human Shape. He can give the understanding\r\nto Men how they may know the Virtues of all\r\nHerbs and Precious Stones. He teacheth the Arts of\r\nLogic and Ethics in all their parts. If desired he maketh\r\nmen invisible, and to live long, and to be eloquent. He can discover Treasures and recover things Lost. He\r\nruleth over 29 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this,\r\nwhich wear thou, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "2a4a661724db13ee884aad9dc372f7d5311e973e1e7c7a33eab6b155a4b75da9",
          "count_context": "nd to be eloquent. He can discover Treasures and recover things Lost. He ruleth over 29 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, which wear thou, etc",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 32,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Asmoday",
          "legions_primary": 72,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 32,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(32.) Asmoday. —The Thirty-second Spirit is Asmoday,\r\nor Asmodai. He is a Great King, Strong, and\r\nPowerful. He appeareth with Three Heads, whereof the\r\nfirst is like a Bull, the second like a Man, and the third\r\nlike a Ram; he hath also the tail of a Serpent, and from\r\nhis mouth issue Flames of Fire. His Feet are webbed\r\nlike those of a Goose. He sitteth upon an Infernal\r\nDragon, and beareth in his hand a Lance with a Banner.\r\nHe is first and choicest under the Power of Amaymon ,\r\nhe goeth before all other. When the Exorcist hath a\r\nmind to call him, let it be abroad, and let him stand on\r\nhis feet all the time of action, with his Cap or Head-dress\r\noff; for if it be on, Amaymon will deceive him and\r\ncall all his actions to be bewrayed. But as soon as the\r\nExorcist seeth Asmoday in the shape aforesaid, he shall\r\ncall him by his Name, saying: “Art thou Asmoday?”\r\nand he will not deny it, and by-and-by he will bow down\r\nunto the ground. He giveth the Ring of Virtues; he\r\nteacheth the Arts of Arithmetic, Astronomy, Geometry,\r\nand all handicrafts absolutely. He giveth true and full\r\nanswers unto thy demands. He maketh one Invincible.\r\nHe showeth the place where Treasures lie, and guardeth\r\nit. He, amongst the Legions of Amaymon governeth 72\r\nLegions of Spirits Inferior. His Seal is this which thou\r\nmust wear as a Lamen upon thy breast, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "4926b3dc2b10fe8b085aab4ce14107ac26d5efae78fe753fa183dc79e52185ac",
          "count_context": "e where Treasures lie, and guardeth it. He, amongst the Legions of Amaymon governeth 72 Legions of Spirits Inferior. His Seal is this which thou must ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 33,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Gaap",
          "legions_primary": 66,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 33,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(33.) Gaap. —The Thirty-third Spirit is Gäap. He is\r\na Great President and a Mighty Prince. He appeareth\r\nwhen the Sun is in some of the Southern Signs, in a\r\nHuman Shape, going before Four Great and Mighty\r\nKings, as if he were a Guide to conduct them along on\r\ntheir way. His Office is to make men Insensible or Ignorant; as also in Philosophy to make them Knowing,\r\nand in all the Liberal Sciences. He can cause Love or\r\nHatred, also he can teach thee to consecrate those things\r\nthat belong to the Dominion of Amaymon his King. He\r\ncan deliver Familiars out of the Custody of other\r\nMagicians, and answereth truly and perfectly of things\r\nPast, Present, and to Come. He can carry and re-carry\r\nmen very speedily from one Kingdom to another, at the\r\nWill and Pleasure of the Exorcist. He ruleth over 66\r\nLegions of Spirits, and he was of the Order of Potentates.\r\nHis Seal is this to be made and to be worn as\r\naforesaid, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "71bcccf5df8ba2eda6cd0aa9035f9ed255cb8d11e5a1c3a0786ac385aa9cb927",
          "count_context": "rom one Kingdom to another, at the Will and Pleasure of the Exorcist. He ruleth over 66 Legions of Spirits, and he was of the Order of Potentates. His",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 34,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Furfur",
          "legions_primary": 26,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 34,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(34.) Furfur. —The Thirty-fourth Spirit is Furfur.\r\nHe is a Great and Mighty Earl, appearing in the Form\r\nof an Hart with a Fiery Tail. He never speaketh truth\r\nunless he be compelled, or brought up within a triangle, △.\r\nBeing therein, he will take upon himself the\r\nForm of an Angel. Being bidden, he speaketh with a\r\nhoarse voice. Also he will wittingly urge Love between\r\nMan and Woman. He can raise Lightnings and Thunders,\r\nBlasts, and Great Tempestuous Storms. And he\r\ngiveth True Answers both of Things Secret and Divine,\r\nif commanded. He ruleth over 26 Legions of Spirits.\r\nAnd his Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "ec7f8eeb5a23a69b14841e186a8aa74fccae7863a9af8d20571303332ea10f79",
          "count_context": "e giveth True Answers both of Things Secret and Divine, if commanded. He ruleth over 26 Legions of Spirits. And his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 35,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Marchosias",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 35,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(35.) Marchosias. —The Thirty-fifth Spirit is Marchosias.\r\nHe is a Great and Mighty Marquis, appearing\r\nat first in the Form of a Wolf having Gryphon’s Wings,\r\nand a Serpent’s Tail, and Vomiting Fire out of his\r\nmouth. But after a time, at the command of the Exorcist\r\nhe putteth on the Shape of a Man. And he is a\r\nstrong fighter. He was of the Order of Dominations.\r\nHe governeth 30 Legions of Spirits. He told his Chief, who was Solomon, that after 1,200 years he had hopes\r\nto return unto the Seventh Throne. And his Seal is this,\r\nto be made and worn as a Lamen, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "2601f0c1cadd8408a49f12946d4f594cfa570765e2a76517275b4e1387378051",
          "count_context": " a Man. And he is a strong fighter. He was of the Order of Dominations. He governeth 30 Legions of Spirits. He told his Chief, who was Solomon, that a",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 36,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Stolas",
          "legions_primary": 26,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 36,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(36.) Stolas, or Stolos. —The Thirty-sixth Spirit is\r\nStolas, or Stolos. He is a Great and Powerful Prince,\r\nappearing in the Shape of a Mighty Raven at first before\r\nthe Exorcist; but after he taketh the image of a Man.\r\nHe teacheth the Art of Astronomy, and the Virtues of\r\nHerbs and Precious Stones. He governeth 26 Legions\r\nof Spirits; and his Seal is this, which is, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "65851aca3554bac684cad7cc9a240d70e18964ad62cbdad60b7803781f95811f",
          "count_context": "eth the Art of Astronomy, and the Virtues of Herbs and Precious Stones. He governeth 26 Legions of Spirits; and his Seal is this, which is, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 37,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Phenex",
          "legions_primary": 20,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 37,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(37.) Phenex. —The Thirty-Seventh Spirit is Phenex\r\n(or Pheynix). He is a great Marquis, and appeareth\r\nlike the Bird Phœnix, having the Voice of a Child. He\r\nsingeth many sweet notes before the Exorcist, which he\r\nmust not regard, but by-and-by he must bid him put on\r\nHuman Shape. Then he will speak marvellously of all\r\nwonderful Sciences if required. He is a Poet, good and\r\nexcellent. And he will be willing to perform thy requests.\r\nHe hath hopes also to return to the Seventh\r\nThrone after 1,200 years more, as he said unto Solomon.\r\nHe governeth 20 Legions of Spirits. And his Seal is\r\nthis, which wear thou, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "9518a5863b3a883f696123b137b2272b429700e9a79d2130c62d694d46d48307",
          "count_context": " to the Seventh Throne after 1,200 years more, as he said unto Solomon. He governeth 20 Legions of Spirits. And his Seal is this, which wear thou, etc",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 38,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Halphas",
          "legions_primary": 26,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 38,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(38.) Halphas , or Malthus .—The Thirty-eighth\r\nSpirit is Halphas, or Malthous (or Malthas). He is a\r\nGreat Earl, and appeareth in the Form of a Stock-Dove.\r\nHe speaketh with a hoarse Voice. His Office is to build\r\nup Towers, and to furnish them with Ammunition and\r\nWeapons, and to send Men-of-War to places appointed.\r\nHe ruleth over 26 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is\r\nthis, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "35fa0208b84b93ba98c191e89367ecdbb7fca15f2cccc2e9ad4d7ac4871279be",
          "count_context": "h Ammunition and Weapons, and to send Men-of-War to places appointed. He ruleth over 26 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 39,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Malphas",
          "legions_primary": 40,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 39,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(39.) Malphas. —The Thirty-ninth Spirit is Malphas.\r\nHe appeareth at first like a Crow, but after he will put\r\non Human Shape at the request of the Exorcist, and speak with a hoarse Voice. He is a Mighty President\r\nand Powerful. He can build Houses and High Towers,\r\nand can bring to thy Knowledge Enemies’ Desires and\r\nThoughts, and that which they have done. He giveth\r\nGood Familiars. If thou makest a Sacrifice unto him he\r\nwill receive it kindly and willingly, but he will deceive\r\nhim that doth it. He governeth 40 Legions of Spirits,\r\nand his Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "a76e9df047eac79af82ebe3d2f96b414e40e8668dc7b9637172f61d12c0b27cd",
          "count_context": " receive it kindly and willingly, but he will deceive him that doth it. He governeth 40 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 40,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Raum",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 40,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(40.) Raum. —The Fortieth Spirit is Räum. He is a\r\nGreat Earl; and appeareth at first in the Form of a\r\nCrow, but after the Command of the Exorcist he putteth\r\non Human Shape. His office is to steal Treasures out\r\nKing’s Houses, and to carry it whither he is commanded,\r\nand to destroy Cities and Dignities of Men, and to tell\r\nall things, Past, and What Is, and what Will Be; and\r\nto cause Love between Friends and Foes. He was of the\r\nOrder of Thrones. He governeth 30 Legions of Spirits;\r\nand his Seal is this, which wear thou as aforesaid.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "b370d6200cf31efee1ea517b4f54f450f7bb17b4d50e2579371e434393fe4eb8",
          "count_context": "to cause Love between Friends and Foes. He was of the Order of Thrones. He governeth 30 Legions of Spirits; and his Seal is this, which wear thou as a",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 41,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Focalor",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 41,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(41.) Focalor. —The Forty-first Spirit is Focalor, or\r\nForcalor, or Furcalor. He is a Mighty Duke and Strong.\r\nHe appeareth in the Form of a Man with Gryphon’s\r\nWings. His office is to slay Men, and to drown them in\r\nthe Waters, and to overthrow Ships of War, for he\r\nhath Power over both Winds and Seas; but he will not\r\nhurt any man or thing if he be commanded to the contrary\r\nby the Exorcist. He also hath hopes to return to\r\nthe Seventh Throne after 1,000 years. He governeth\r\n30 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "4cefcc6a55fa69e065e59d6de9559fe3e96b6933608ed30423257280864a98f2",
          "count_context": ". He also hath hopes to return to the Seventh Throne after 1,000 years. He governeth 30 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 42,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Vepar",
          "legions_primary": 29,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 42,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(42.) Vepar. —The Forty-second Spirit is Vepar, or\r\nVephar. He is a Duke Great and Strong and appeareth\r\nlike a Mermaid. His office is to govern the Waters, and\r\nto guide Ships laden with Arms, Armour, and Ammunition,\r\netc., thereon. And at the request of the Exorcist\r\nhe can cause the seas to be right stormy and to appear full of ships. Also he maketh men to die in Three Days\r\nby Putrefying Wounds or Sores, and causing Worms to\r\nbreed in them. He governeth 29 Legions of Spirits, and\r\nhis Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "de16ef2df750f1d2d378ac682209759a88b0bdeaedfb5d3b29c5ba12a3b48663",
          "count_context": "Days by Putrefying Wounds or Sores, and causing Worms to breed in them. He governeth 29 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 43,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Sabnock",
          "legions_primary": 50,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 43,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(43.) Sabnock. —The Forty-third Spirit, as King\r\nSolomon commanded them into the Vessel of Brass, is\r\ncalled Sabnock, or Savnok. He is a Marquis, Mighty,\r\nGreat and Strong, appearing in the Form of an Armed\r\nSoldier with a Lion’s Head, riding on a pale-coloured\r\nhorse. His office is to build high Towers, Castles and\r\nCities, and to furnish them with Armour, etc. Also he\r\ncan afflict Men for many days with Wounds and with\r\nSores rotten and full of Worms. He giveth Good Familiars\r\nat the request of the Exorcist. He commandeth\r\n50 Legions of Spirits; and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "49c6b917804691b90dc6230d0c4771f7281f586987bcea624fbe5e6c24c1b4a7",
          "count_context": "ull of Worms. He giveth Good Familiars at the request of the Exorcist. He commandeth 50 Legions of Spirits; and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 44,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Shax",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 44,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(44.) Shax. —The Forty-fourth Spirit is Shax, or\r\nShaz (or Shass). He is a Great Marquis and appeareth\r\nin the Form of a Stock-Dove, speaking with a voice\r\nhoarse, but yet subtle. His Office is to take away the\r\nSight, Hearing, or Understanding of any Man or Woman\r\nat the command of the Exorcist; and to steal money out\r\nof the houses of Kings, and to carry it again in 1,200\r\nyears. If commanded he will fetch Horses at the request\r\nof the Exorcist, or any other thing. But he must first\r\nbe commanded into a Triangle, △, or else he will deceive\r\nhim, and tell him many Lies. He can discover all things\r\nthat are Hidden, and not kept by Wicked Spirits. He\r\ngiveth good Familiars, sometimes. He governeth 30\r\nLegions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "2adc6fdbba59fc71fa9e4f769fcd824bce794d1b1d710185ab1b8c0486da10a9",
          "count_context": "n, and not kept by Wicked Spirits. He giveth good Familiars, sometimes. He governeth 30 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 45,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Vine",
          "legions_primary": 36,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 45,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(45.) Viné. —The Forty-fifth Spirit is Viné, or Vinea.\r\nHe is a Great King, and an Earl; and appeareth in the\r\nForm of a Lion, riding upon a Black Horse, and bearing a Viper in his hand. His Office is to discover Things\r\nHidden, Witches, Wizards, and Things Present, Past,\r\nand to Come. He, at the command of the Exorcist will\r\nbuild Towers, overthrow Great Stone Walls, and make\r\nthe Waters rough with Storms. He governeth 36 Legions\r\nof Spirits. And his Seal is this, which wear thou,\r\nas aforesaid, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "2cba963a0f4a2e064c9a969c22e0e137f622fe5d3c0c7e81d9f2feba917328bf",
          "count_context": "rs, overthrow Great Stone Walls, and make the Waters rough with Storms. He governeth 36 Legions of Spirits. And his Seal is this, which wear thou, as ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 46,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Bifrons",
          "legions_primary": 6,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 46,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(46.) Bifrons. —The Forty-sixth Spirit is called\r\nBifrons, or Bifröus, or Bifrovs. He is an Earl, and\r\nappeareth in the Form of a Monster; but after a while,\r\nat the Command of the Exorcist, he putteth on the shape\r\nof a Man. His Office is to make one knowing in Astrology,\r\nGeometry, and other Arts and Sciences. He teacheth\r\nthe Virtues of Precious Stones and Woods. He\r\nchangeth Dead Bodies, and putteth them in another\r\nplace; also he lighteth seeming Candles upon the Graves\r\nof the Dead. He hath under his Command 6 Legions\r\nof Spirits. His Seal is this, which he will own and submit\r\nunto, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "92eb556f5ce23f2c1778874468f2934500a9b259cfb7a472ec4b87e4f59155de",
          "count_context": "o he lighteth seeming Candles upon the Graves of the Dead. He hath under his Command 6 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, which he will own and su",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 47,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Vual",
          "legions_primary": 37,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 47,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(47.) Uvall , Vual , or Voval .—The Forty-seventh\r\nSpirit is Uvall, or Vual, or Voval. He is a Duke, Great,\r\nMighty, and Strong; and appeareth in the Form of a\r\nMighty Dromedary at the first, but after a while at the\r\nCommand of the Exorcist he putteth on Human Shape,\r\nand speaketh the Egyptian Tongue, but not perfectly. His Office is to procure the Love of Woman, and to tell\r\nThings Past, Present, and to Come. He also procureth\r\nFriendship between Friends and Foes. He was of the\r\nOrder of Potestates or Powers. He governeth 37 Legions\r\nof Spirits, and his Seal is this, to be made and worn\r\nbefore thee, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "3056c8915e77b0f8db098f7913483de537078c179884589cd7d21ca5263a2f07",
          "count_context": " between Friends and Foes. He was of the Order of Potestates or Powers. He governeth 37 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, to be made and worn ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 48,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Haagenti",
          "legions_primary": 33,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 48,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(48.) Haagenti. —The Forty-eighth Spirit is Haagenti.\r\nHe is a President, appearing in the Form of a Mighty\r\nBull with Gryphon’s Wings. This is at first, but after,\r\nat the Command of the Exorcist he putteth on Human\r\nShape. His Office is to make Men wise, and to instruct\r\nthem in divers things; also to Transmute all Metals into\r\nGold; and to change Wine into Water, and Water into\r\nWine. He governeth 33 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal\r\nis this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "702e736cdec8d9bb8dbaba364252c6a12d3fe4f72a63a804d8e8aeb1f549ed0f",
          "count_context": "l Metals into Gold; and to change Wine into Water, and Water into Wine. He governeth 33 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 49,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Crocell",
          "legions_primary": 48,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 49,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(49.) Crocell. —The Forty-ninth Spirit is Crocell, or\r\nCrokel. He appeareth in the Form of an Angel. He is\r\na Duke Great and Strong, speaking something Mystically\r\nof Hidden Things. He teacheth the Art of Geometry\r\nand the Liberal Sciences. He, at the Command of the\r\nExorcist, will produce Great Noises like the Rushings\r\nof many Waters, although there be none. He warmeth\r\nWaters, and discovereth Baths. He was of the Order of\r\nPotestates, or Powers, before his fall, as he declared unto\r\nthe King Solomon. He governeth 48 Legions of Spirits.\r\nHis Seal is this, the which wear thou as aforesaid.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "0df4012dc94d54303fbb3543354f1f9841ae71027887b52f9761d0bcedce3441",
          "count_context": "ates, or Powers, before his fall, as he declared unto the King Solomon. He governeth 48 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, the which wear thou as a",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 50,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Furcas",
          "legions_primary": 20,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 50,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(50.) Furcas. —The Fiftieth Spirit is Furcas. He is\r\na Knight, and appeareth in the Form of a Cruel Old Man\r\nwith a long Beard and a hoary Head, riding upon a pale-coloured\r\nHorse, with a Sharp Weapon in his hand. His\r\nOffice is to teach the Arts of Philosophy, Astrology,\r\nRhetoric, Logic, Cheiromancy, and Pyromancy, in all\r\ntheir parts, and perfectly. He hath under his Power 20\r\nLegions of Spirits. His Seal, or Mark, is thus made, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "7063b017979001a5ffbd3f50e552700f7882d7ae87c21f3dd639e06fdab2e08c",
          "count_context": "eiromancy, and Pyromancy, in all their parts, and perfectly. He hath under his Power 20 Legions of Spirits. His Seal, or Mark, is thus made, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 51,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Balam",
          "legions_primary": 40,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 51,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(51.) Balam. —The Fifty-first Spirit is Balam or\r\nBalaam. He is a Terrible, Great, and Powerful King.\r\nHe appeareth with three Heads: the first is like that of\r\na Bull; the second is like that of a Man; the third is like\r\nthat of a Ram. He hath the Tail of a Serpent, and\r\nFlaming Eyes. He rideth upon a furious Bear, and carrieth a Boshawk upon his Fist. He speaketh with a\r\nhoarse Voice, giving True Answers of Things Past, Present,\r\nand to Come. He maketh men to go Invisible, and\r\nalso to be Witty. He governeth 40 Legions of Spirits.\r\nHis Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "1e2bf2bad28453ad532e84efc0225f9c73fab89f83a0c08ba569066b69f677ec",
          "count_context": "sent, and to Come. He maketh men to go Invisible, and also to be Witty. He governeth 40 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 52,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Alloces",
          "legions_primary": 36,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 52,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(52.) Alloces. —The Fifty-second Spirit is Alloces,\r\nor Alocas. He is a Duke, Great, Mighty, and Strong,\r\nappearing in the Form of a Soldier riding upon a Great\r\nHorse. His Face is like that of a Lion, very Red, and\r\nhaving Flaming Eyes. His Speech is hoarse and very\r\nbig. His Office is to teach the Art of Astronomy, and\r\nall the Liberal Sciences. He bringeth unto thee Good\r\nFamiliars; also he ruleth over 36 Legions of Spirits.\r\nHis Seal is this, which, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "573894e3038e93cf4e24f131cc5912bfa548fec40f86d085cdde4759b249119d",
          "count_context": " all the Liberal Sciences. He bringeth unto thee Good Familiars; also he ruleth over 36 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, which, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 53,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Caim",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 53,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(53.) Camio or Caim .—The Fifty-third Spirit is\r\nCamio, or Caim. He is a Great President, and appeareth\r\nin the Form of the Bird called a Thrush at first, but\r\nafterwards he putteth on the Shape of a Man carrying\r\nin his Hand a Sharp Sword. He seemeth to answer in\r\nBurning Ashes, or in Coals of Fire. He is a Good Disputer.\r\nHis Office is to give unto Men the Understanding\r\nof all Birds, Lowing of Bullocks, Barking of Dogs,\r\nand other Creatures; and also of the Voice of the Waters.\r\nHe giveth True Answers of Things to Come. He was\r\nof the Order of Angels, but now ruleth over 30 Legions\r\nof Spirits Infernal. His Seal is this, which wear thou,\r\netc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "1dc53381695a0a777c1cf2f06c138746b64a960c164ac8779d26472ddb1ca2d6",
          "count_context": "h True Answers of Things to Come. He was of the Order of Angels, but now ruleth over 30 Legions of Spirits Infernal. His Seal is this, which wear thou",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 54,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Murmur",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 54,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(54.) Murmur , or Murmus .—The Fifty-fourth Spirit\r\nis called Murmur, or Murmus, or Murmux. He is a\r\nGreat Duke, and an Earl; and appeareth in the Form of\r\na Warrior riding upon a Gryphon, with a Ducal Crown\r\nupon his Head. There do go before him those his Ministers with great Trumpets sounding. His Office is to\r\nteach Philosophy perfectly, and to constrain Souls Deceased\r\nto come before the Exorcist to answer those questions\r\nwhich he may wish to put to them, if desired. He\r\nwas partly of the Order of Thrones, and partly of that\r\nof Angels. He now ruleth 30 Legions of Spirits. And\r\nhis Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "81cd422c7f840c443376672442697b6f9adfd88d64205f8b3f561460f03a742a",
          "count_context": ". He was partly of the Order of Thrones, and partly of that of Angels. He now ruleth 30 Legions of Spirits. And his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 55,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Orobas",
          "legions_primary": 20,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 55,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(55.) Orobas. —The Fifty-fifth Spirit is Orobas. He\r\nis a great and Mighty Prince, appearing at first like a\r\nHorse; but after the command of the Exorcist he putteth\r\non the Image of a Man. His Office is to discover all\r\nthings Past, Present, and to Come; also to give Dignities,\r\nand Prelacies, and the Favour of Friends and of\r\nFoes. He giveth True Answers of Divinity, and of the\r\nCreation of the World. He is very faithful unto the\r\nExorcist, and will not suffer him to be tempted of any\r\nSpirit. He governeth 20 Legions of Spirits. His Seal\r\nis this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "e1dcaa223f31db0651aca58c5c4a2e24081d70b3ac0b13009b0c486f2313fe6f",
          "count_context": "unto the Exorcist, and will not suffer him to be tempted of any Spirit. He governeth 20 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
