            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(56.) Gremory , or Gamori .—The Fifty-sixth Spirit\r\nis Gremory, or Gamori. He is a Duke Strong and Powerful,\r\nand appeareth in the Form of a Beautiful Woman,\r\nwith a Duchess’s Crown tied about her waist, and riding\r\non a Great Camel. His Office is to tell of all Things\r\nPast, Present, and to Come; and of Treasures Hid, and\r\nwhat they lie in; and to procure the Love of Women\r\nboth Young and Old. He governeth 26 Legions of\r\nSpirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "cdc6fc72dea364ea811bf728b5970899eb6a85607857da5216b2b482429fa039",
          "count_context": " what they lie in; and to procure the Love of Women both Young and Old. He governeth 26 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
