            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(63.) Andras. —The Sixty-third Spirit is Andras.\r\nHe is a Great Marquis, appearing in the Form of an\r\nAngel with a Head like a Black Night Raven, riding\r\nupon a strong Black Wolf, and having a Sharp and\r\nBright Sword flourished aloft in his hand. His Office is\r\nto sow Discords. If the Exorcist have not a care, he will\r\nslay both him and his fellows. He governeth 30 Legions\r\nof Spirits, and this is his Seal, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "cabd9b29c95d04372304c02434de755dfac03e13320d193a4e73fd947a3b58fc",
          "count_context": "If the Exorcist have not a care, he will slay both him and his fellows. He governeth 30 Legions of Spirits, and this is his Seal, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 64,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Flauros",
          "legions_primary": 36,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 64,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(64.) Haures , or Hauras , or Havres , or Flauros .—The\r\nSixty-fourth Spirit is Haures, or Hauras, or Havres,\r\nor Flauros. He is a Great Duke, and appeareth at first\r\nlike a Leopard, Mighty, Terrible, and Strong, but after\r\na while, at the Command of the Exorcist, he putteth on\r\nHuman Shape with Eyes Flaming and Fiery, and a most Terrible Countenance. He giveth True Answers\r\nof all things, Present, Past, and to Come. But if he be\r\nnot commanded into a Triangle, △, he will Lie in all\r\nthese Things, and deceive and beguile the Exorcist in\r\nthese things, or in such and such business. He will,\r\nlastly, talk of the Creation of the World, and of Divinity,\r\nand of how he and other Spirits fell. He destroyeth\r\nand burneth up those who be the Enemies of the Exorcist\r\nshould he so desire it; also he will not suffer him\r\nto be tempted by any other Spirit or otherwise. He\r\ngoverneth 36 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, to\r\nbe worn as a Lamen, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "6b11496d8e98008ca2898b3ce74b6b5e18d175c744e5a6823405bf24b3b4ad25",
          "count_context": " he will not suffer him to be tempted by any other Spirit or otherwise. He governeth 36 Legions of Spirits, and his Seal is this, to be worn as a Lame",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 65,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Andrealphus",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 65,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(65.) Andrealphus. —The Sixty-fifth Spirit is Andrealphus.\r\nHe is a Mighty Marquis, appearing at first in\r\nthe form of a Peacock, with great Noises. But after a\r\ntime he putteth on Human shape. He can teach Geometry\r\nperfectly. He maketh Men very subtle therein;\r\nand in all Things pertaining unto Mensuration or Astronomy.\r\nHe can transform a Man into the Likeness\r\nof a Bird. He governeth 30 Legions of Infernal Spirits,\r\nand his Seal is this, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "b5385c0e97ae68a83c4a68687d6f0aa2944f4cc57f36657e2a1d818900cbf6eb",
          "count_context": "ation or Astronomy. He can transform a Man into the Likeness of a Bird. He governeth 30 Legions of Infernal Spirits, and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 66,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Cimejes",
          "legions_primary": 20,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 66,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(66.) Cimejes , or Cimeies , or Kimaris .—The Sixty-sixth\r\nSpirit is Cimejes, or Cimeies, or Kimaris. He is a\r\nMarquis, Mighty, Great, Strong and Powerful, appearing\r\nlike a Valiant Warrior riding upon a goodly Black\r\nHorse. He ruleth over all Spirits in the parts of Africa.\r\nHis Office is to teach perfectly Grammar, Logic, Rhetoric,\r\nand to discover things Lost or Hidden, and Treasures.\r\nHe governeth 20 Legions of Infernals; and his Seal is\r\nthis, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "ec9343e1b1f18feb75d2f027e960fcd51337fd93d5568d419198573d01983690",
          "count_context": " Logic, Rhetoric, and to discover things Lost or Hidden, and Treasures. He governeth 20 Legions of Infernals; and his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 67,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Amdusias",
          "legions_primary": 29,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 67,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(67.) Amdusias , or Amdukias .—The Sixty-seventh\r\nSpirit is Amdusias, or Amdukias. He is a Duke Great\r\nand Strong, appearing at first like a Unicorn, but at the\r\nrequest of the Exorcist he standeth before him in Human Shape, causing Trumpets, and all manner of Musical\r\nInstruments to be heard, but not soon or immediately.\r\nAlso he can cause Trees to bend and incline according\r\nto the Exorcist’s Will. He giveth Excellent Familiars.\r\nHe governeth 29 Legions of Spirits. And his Seal is\r\nthis, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "7724400c0a013812384f9a3e9ef46385a33dc7be54543ceaa65164ba55245b48",
          "count_context": "ncline according to the Exorcist’s Will. He giveth Excellent Familiars. He governeth 29 Legions of Spirits. And his Seal is this, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 68,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Belial",
          "legions_primary": 50,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 68,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(68.) Belial. —The Sixty-eighth Spirit is Belial. He\r\nis a Mighty and a Powerful King, and was created next\r\nafter Lucifer . He appeareth in the Form of Two Beautiful\r\nAngels sitting in a Chariot of Fire. He speaketh\r\nwith a Comely Voice, and declareth that he fell first from\r\namong the worthier sort, that were before Michael, and\r\nother Heavenly Angels. His Office is to distribute Presentations\r\nand Senatorships, etc.; and to cause favour of\r\nFriends and of Foes. He giveth excellent Familiars,\r\nand governeth 50 Legions of Spirits. Note well that\r\nthis King Belial must have Offerings, Sacrifices and\r\nGifts presented unto him by the Exorcist, or else he will\r\nnot give True Answers unto his Demands. But then he\r\ntarrieth not one hour in the Truth, unless he be constrained\r\nby Divine Power. And his Seal is this, which is\r\nto be worn as aforesaid, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "65d9428734fcc45253bebc86ec70ab5774dc081ec517486c84e72fd4922c8bb7",
          "count_context": "to cause favour of Friends and of Foes. He giveth excellent Familiars, and governeth 50 Legions of Spirits. Note well that this King Belial must have ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 69,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Decarabia",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 69,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(69.) Decarabia. —The Sixty-ninth Spirit is Decarabia.\r\nHe appeareth in the Form of a Star in a Pentacle,\r\nat first; but after, at the command of the Exorcist, he\r\nputteth on the image of a Man. His Office is to discover\r\nthe Virtues of Birds and Precious Stones, and to make\r\nthe Similitude of all kinds of Birds to fly before the\r\nExorcist, singing and drinking as natural Birds do. He\r\ngoverneth 30 Legions of Spirits, being himself a Great\r\nMarquis. And this is his Seal, which is to be worn, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "2bf681a27ed38cd711410dc0882a44be272917d4efaa9cdfeaa61cabef0b8d3f",
          "count_context": "s to fly before the Exorcist, singing and drinking as natural Birds do. He governeth 30 Legions of Spirits, being himself a Great Marquis. And this is",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 70,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Seere",
          "legions_primary": 26,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 70,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(70.) Seere , Sear , or Seir .—The Seventieth Spirit is\r\nSeere, Sear, or Seir. He is a Mighty Prince, and Powerful,\r\nunder Amaymon , King of the East. He appeareth in the Form of a Beautiful Man, riding upon a Winged\r\nHorse. His Office is to go and come; and to bring abundance\r\nof things to pass on a sudden, and to carry or recarry\r\nanything whither thou wouldest have it to go, or\r\nwhence thou wouldest have it from. He can pass over\r\nthe whole Earth in the twinkling of an Eye. He giveth\r\na True relation of all sorts of Theft, and of Treasure hid,\r\nand of many other things. He is of an indifferent Good\r\nNature, and is willing to do anything which the Exorcist\r\ndesireth. He governeth 26 Legions of Spirits. And this\r\nhis Seal is to be worn, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "cf1ecdd9526883f592778754a0b17e6cc5fc1e8ee2f59cf49141540ac47df6c0",
          "count_context": "Good Nature, and is willing to do anything which the Exorcist desireth. He governeth 26 Legions of Spirits. And this his Seal is to be worn, etc.",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 71,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Dantalion",
          "legions_primary": 36,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 71,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(71.) Dantalion. —The Seventy-first Spirit is Dantalion.\r\nHe is a Duke Great and Mighty, appearing in\r\nthe Form of a Man with many Countenances, all Men’s\r\nand Women’s Faces; and he hath a Book in his right\r\nhand. His Office is to teach all Arts and Sciences unto\r\nany; and to declare the Secret Counsel of any one; for\r\nhe knoweth the Thoughts of all Men and Women, and\r\ncan change them at his Will. He can cause Love, and\r\nshow the Similitude of any person, and show the same\r\nby a Vision, let them be in what part of the World they\r\nWill. He governeth 36 Legions of Spirits; and this is\r\nhis Seal, which wear thou, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "9c8721513d923ec929da6c3615912aaa3b4717a4b402c13a56542f6890363918",
          "count_context": " the same by a Vision, let them be in what part of the World they Will. He governeth 36 Legions of Spirits; and this is his Seal, which wear thou, etc",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 72,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Andromalius",
          "legions_primary": 36,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 72,
            "paragraph_id": null,
            "section": "SHEMHAMPHORASH",
            "main_cell": false
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "(72.) Andromalius. —The Seventy-second Spirit in\r\nOrder is named Andromalius. He is an Earl, Great and\r\nMighty, appearing in the Form of a Man holding a\r\nGreat Serpent in his Hand. His Office is to bring back\r\nboth a Thief, and the Goods which be stolen; and to discover\r\nall Wickedness, and Underhand Dealing; and to\r\npunish all Thieves and other Wicked People and also to\r\ndiscover Treasures that be Hid. He ruleth over 36\r\nLegions of Spirits. His Seal is this, the which wear thou\r\nas aforesaid, etc.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "201b48536a22a21e920ab39e95a4b0ee71daf8526afbd1759600cdd0d63508fb",
          "count_context": "s and other Wicked People and also to discover Treasures that be Hid. He ruleth over 36 Legions of Spirits. His Seal is this, the which wear thou as a",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        }
      ],
      "goetia_peterson_sloane3825": [
        {
