            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 28 spirit in order as salomon bound them, is named Berith . he is a Mighty great and terrable duke,\nhe hath two other Names given to him by men of latter Times, viz: Beal & Bolfry , he appeareth like a\nsouldier w red clothing, ridding on a red horse & \na Crown of Gold upon his head he giveth True answards of things, \npast present & to come; you [must] use a Ring as is\nbefore spoken of Beleth in calling him forth; he can turne all mettals\ninto Gold, he can give dignity & confirm them to Men, he speaketh\nw a very clear & subtill voice, he is a great Lyer and not to\nbe Trusted much he governeth over 26 Legions of spirits his seal is this\nwhich must be worne as [a] lamin.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "0a96492bd515fd7f4fcb3490e4f284997f9908eaf69a76f0593dc48f8dcaae3f",
          "count_context": "ear & subtill voice, he is a great Lyer and not to be Trusted much he governeth over 26 Legions of spirits his seal is this which must be worne as lam",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 29,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Astaroth",
          "legions_primary": 40,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 29,
            "paragraph_id": "astaroth",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 29 spirit in order is Named Astaroth , he is a Mighty & strong duke and appeareth in [the] forme of an\nunbeautifull angel, ridding on an Infernall like dragon, and carring\nin his right hand a viper (you must not lett him come to neare y least he doe y damage by his stinking Breath. Therefore\ny Exorcist must hold y Magicall Ring nere to his face\nand y will defend him he giveth true answares of things present\npast & to come & can discover all secreets; he will declare willingly\nhow y spirits fell, if desired, & y reason of his\nown fall. He can make men wounderfull knowing in all Liberall siences; he\nrules 40 Legions of spirits, his seal is this, w weare as a Lamen before y , or else he w not obey you.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "18d70b764f72093a395988df016355b2665044dd4abe8080ab03ecd91872aabc",
          "count_context": " his own fall. He can make men wounderfull knowing in all Liberall siences; he rules 40 Legions of spirits, his seal is this, w weare as a Lamen befor",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
