          "imported_comparison_name": "Forneus",
          "legions_primary": 29,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 30,
            "paragraph_id": "forneus",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 30 spirit is called Forneus , he is a\nmighty great Marquiz, & appeareth in y forme of a great\nsea Monster, he Teacheth & maketh men wounderfull knowing in y art of Rhetoric he causeth men to have a good Name, and to have y understanding of Tongues; he maketh men to be beloved of their foes as well as\nthey bee by their friends; & he governeth 29 Legions of spirits,\npartly of y order of Thrones and partly of angels, his seal\nis this to be made and worne as aforesaid &c.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "b56d7f21c7dafca505204223d9c2e9daa5a046dab651e77f97c8a3a176659c4e",
          "count_context": "men to be beloved of their foes as well as they bee by their friends; & he governeth 29 Legions of spirits, partly of y order of Thrones and partly of",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
