            "paragraph_id": "foras",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 31 spirit in order, is named Foras , he is a mighty great president & appeareth in y form of a \nstrong man, in humane shape he can give y understanding \nto men how they may know y vertues of all hearbs and precious \nstones, & teacheth them y art [of] Logick & \nEthicks in All their partes if desired, he maketh men Invisible, witty, \nEloquent & to live Long; he [can] discover Treasures and recover Things \nlost, & he ruleth over 29 Legions of spirits, his seale or Character \nis thus to be made & worne as a Lamen.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "40bcc2542a364dfe24b42e5583e6f9128aa8bd30d4a8ba5f2f9f48afd964914d",
          "count_context": "uent & to live Long; he discover Treasures and recover Things lost, & he ruleth over 29 Legions of spirits, his seale or Character is thus to be made ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 32,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Asmoday",
          "legions_primary": 72,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 32,
            "paragraph_id": "asmoday",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 32 spirit in order is called Asmoday . he is a great king, strong & powerfull; he appeareth w 3\nheads, whereof y first is like a Bull The second like a\nMan, The Third like a Ram, [he appeareth also] w a serpents\nTaile, Belching or vomitting up flames of fire out of his mouth\nhis feet are webed like a Goose, he sitteth on an Infernall dragon\ncarring a Launce and a flagg in his hands, he is y first\n& chifiest under y power of Amaymon ,\n& goeth before all others: when the [105r] Exorcist hath a mind to call him, lett it be abroad , and lett him stand\non his feet all y Time of action, w his cap of [off] , for if it be on, Amaymon will deceive him, and cause all his doeing\nto be bewrayed, But as soone as y Exorist [Exorcist] seeth\nAsmoday in y shape aforesaid, he shall call him by his Name,\nsaying, thou art Asmoday, & he will not deny it; \nand by & by he will bow down to y grownd &c he giveth y Ring of vertues he teacheth y art of Arithmitick, geomitry, \nAstronomy, and all handicrafts absolutly; he giveth full and \nTrue answares to y demands, he maketh a man Invisible, he showeth\ny place where Treasures layeth, and guardeth it if it be among\ny Legions of Amaymon, he governeth 72 Legions of Inferiour spirits,\nhis seal is thus, to be made and worne as a Lamen before [thee] on your Breast.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "c57be8f5bae4b6ff31ddcc1bb44fb52a07a67fe13b5178a401baf596c79905ab",
          "count_context": " Treasures layeth, and guardeth it if it be among y Legions of Amaymon, he governeth 72 Legions of Inferiour spirits, his seal is thus, to be made and",
