            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 65 spirit is called Andrealphus , he is a Mighty great\nMarquiz appearing at first in y forme of [a] Peacock,\nw great Noises but afterward he putteth on humane \nshape, he can teach perfectly geomitry, & all Things belonging\nto measuring, also Astronomy, he maketh men very subtile and\ncunning therin, he can Transforme a Man into y likness of a\nBird & he governeth 30 Legions of spirits his seal is This, w is to be worne as a Lamin &c.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "66d5d972c53e2b71e9b470e414c1707983daaae9d21a4e8ad0df8e8b6c9090ef",
          "count_context": " and cunning therin, he can Transforme a Man into y likness of a Bird & he governeth 30 Legions of spirits his seal is This, w is to be worne as a Lam",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 66,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Cimejes",
          "legions_primary": 20,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 66,
            "paragraph_id": "cimeies",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 66 spirit is called Cimeies he is a\nmighty great Marquiz strong & powerfull appearing like a valiant\nsouldier, riding on a goodly Black horse; he ruleth over all spirits\nin y part[s] of Africa, his office is to Teach perfectly grammar\nRhetoric [&] logick and to discover Treasures & Things lost or hidden,\nhe can make a man seeme like a souldier of his own likness, he\ngoverneth 20 Legions of cheefe spirits, but more Inferior then himself his seal \nis Thus made, & worne as a Lamin &c.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "25c0faac8dfe6d75407dc6b1ff5fbef0c35501e1681e3bf318a6b394a15ca240",
          "count_context": " or hidden, he can make a man seeme like a souldier of his own likness, he governeth 20 Legions of cheefe spirits, but more Inferior then himself his ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 67,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Amdusias",
          "legions_primary": 29,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 67,
            "paragraph_id": "amduscias",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 67 spirit in order is called Amduscias , he is a strong & great duke appearing at first like an Unicorne,\nBut afterwards at y Request of y Exorcist he standeth [110r] before him in humane shape causing Trumpets and all manner of Musicall\nInstruments to be heard But not seene also [causing] Trees to bend\nand Incline according to y Exorcist [Exorcist's] will; he giveth\nExcellent familiars & ruleth 29 Legions of spirits his seal is Thus formed\n& is to be w as a Lamin &c.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "30acadce193d01ab24f312bda439655c213ad264ce0f9f667b22c44922253523",
          "count_context": "end and Incline according to y Exorcist will; he giveth Excellent familiars & ruleth 29 Legions of spirits his seal is Thus formed & is to be w as a L",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 68,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Belial",
          "legions_primary": 80,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 68,
            "paragraph_id": "belial",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 68 spirit is called Belial , he is a\nmighty king and powerfull; he was Created next after Lucifer, &\nis of his order; he appeareth in y forme of a Beautiful angel\nsitting in a Charriot of fire, speaking w a comly voice,\ndeclaring that he fell first & amongst y worthier & wiser\nsort w went before Michael & other heavenly angels; his\noffice is to distribute preferments of senatorships, and to cause\nfavour of friends & foes, he giveth Excellent familiars & governeth\n80 Legions of spirits. Note this kink [! *king] Belial must have offerings\nsacrafices & gifts presented to him, by y Exorcist or else\nhe w not give True answares to his demands; But then he\nTarryeth not one hour in y truth except he \nbe constrained by devine power & his seal is Thus w is to be\nworne as a Lamin, before y Exorcist &c.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "0d38aec6a093998c1e012668c8e6c0bb41dd4eb28044830373a7a69834821734",
          "count_context": "ps, and to cause favour of friends & foes, he giveth Excellent familiars & governeth 80 Legions of spirits. Note this kink Belial must have offerings ",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 69,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Decarabia",
          "legions_primary": 30,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 69,
            "paragraph_id": "decarabia",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 69 spirit is called Decarabia , he appeareth in\ny forme of a starre in y Pentacle at first, but\nafterwards at y command of y Exorcist, he putteth on\ny Image of a man, his office is to discover y vertues\nof hearbes and precious stones; and to make y similitude of all \nBirds to fly before y Exorcist, & to Tarry w him,\nsinging and Drinking as Naturall Birds doe, he governeth 30 Legions of\nspirits, being himselfe a great Marquiz, his seal is Thus to be made, and\nworne as a Lamin before y Exorcist &.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "4b2fb0c915880c2124fa437c9c89197e9c78c9058f026910ed5b03821bd7eaf5",
          "count_context": "Exorcist, & to Tarry w him, singing and Drinking as Naturall Birds doe, he governeth 30 Legions of spirits, being himselfe a great Marquiz, his seal i",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 70,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Seere",
          "legions_primary": 26,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 70,
            "paragraph_id": "seere",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 70 spirit in order is called Seere , he\nis a Mighty Prince and powerfull under Amaymon, king of y East\nhe appeareth in y forme of a Beautifull Man, riding on a strong\nhorse w wings: his office is to goe & come, and to bring all\nThings to pass on a sudden & to carry & recarry any Thing where\nThou wilt have it, or have it from for he can pass over y whole\nworld in y Twinckling of an Eye, he maketh a True relation of\nall sorts of Theft and of [110v] Treasures hidd, and of all other things, he is Indifferent good Natured,\nwilling to do any thing y Exorcist desireth; he governeth 26\nLegions of spirits, his Mark or seal is Thus made, and is to be worne as a\nLamin &c.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "42b9c7d588f0615798ac60e1d4374dc419fbc40ba946d8bace7fb7776b73bc31",
          "count_context": " Indifferent good Natured, willing to do any thing y Exorcist desireth; he governeth 26 Legions of spirits, his Mark or seal is Thus made, and is to b",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
        {
          "position": 71,
          "imported_comparison_name": "Dantalion",
          "legions_primary": 36,
          "additional_accompanying_legions": null,
          "selector": {
            "catalogue_position": 71,
            "paragraph_id": "dantalion",
            "section": "catalog",
            "main_cell": true
          },
          "source_text_with_editorial_brackets": "The 71 spirit is called Dantalion , he is a great & Mighty\nduke appearing in y forme of a Man w many faces, all\nlike men & women, & a Booke in his right hand; his office is to Teach\nall arts and siences to anyone, and to declare y secreet Councelles\nof anyone, for he knoweth y Thoughts of all men and women, and can\nchange them at his will, he can cause love and shew (by vision) y true similitude of anyone lett them be in w place or part of\ny world they will, he governeth 36 Legions of spirits his seal is\nThis, w is to be worne as a Lamin.",
          "extracted_main_text_sha256": "7a5afcdcc990883029a922f7f4d5f99cdea4478da57fa30f53c39797fed30d9c",
          "count_context": "ilitude of anyone lett them be in w place or part of y world they will, he governeth 36 Legions of spirits his seal is This, w is to be worne as a Lam",
          "count_policy": "Remove superscript footnote markers and bracketed editorial alternatives for this main reading; choose first direct legion count. Retain brackets/source separately. Paimon secondary25 remains separately typed."
        },
